kg/(m·s)|Pa·s">kg/(m·s) = Pa·s</button><button data-unit-example="J/s|W">J/s = W</button><button data-unit-example="g/cm³|kg/m³">g/cm³ = kg/m³</button></div><button class="primary" data-dim-check="" style="margin-top:14px">Check dimensions →</button><div class="dimension-result dim-result">Enter units and check compatibility.</div><p class="local-disclaimer">This checks dimensional equivalence and conversion scale. Temperature factors compare intervals; absolute Celsius/Fahrenheit values require offsets. It does not validate whether units are appropriate for a particular equation.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="page" id="formulas"><div class="page-view"><div class="page-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">REFERENCE</div><h1>Formula library</h1><p>Search engineering equations, variable meanings, SI units, and assumptions.</p></div></div><div class="formula-filters"><input class="search-input" id="formulaSearch" placeholder="Search formulas, variables, or topics"><div class="filter-select" id="formulaCount">22 formulas</div></div><div class="formula-list" id="formulaList"><article class="card formula-card"><h3>General conservation balance <span class="formula-category">Material &amp; energy balances</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">Accumulation = In − Out + Generation − Consumption</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Accumulation</td><td>Rate of change inside the system</td><td>quantity/time</td></tr><tr><td>In, Out</td><td>Input and output rates</td><td>quantity/time</td></tr><tr><td>Generation, Consumption</td><td>Reaction source and sink rates</td><td>quantity/time</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Choose a control volume and a consistent sign convention. At steady state, accumulation is zero.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="General conservation balance" data-pw-title="General conservation balance" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Component mass balance <span class="formula-category">Material &amp; energy balances</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">ṁ_A = ṁ w_A</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ṁ_A</td><td>Component A mass flow rate</td><td>kg/s</td></tr><tr><td>ṁ</td><td>Total stream mass flow rate</td><td>kg/s</td></tr><tr><td>w_A</td><td>Component A mass fraction</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For a mixture, mass fractions sum to one. Use mole fractions with molar flow rates for molar balances.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Component mass balance" data-pw-title="Component mass balance" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Single-reactant conversion <span class="formula-category">Reaction engineering</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">X_A = (n_A,0 − n_A) / n_A,0</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>X_A</td><td>Fraction of A reacted</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>n_A,0</td><td>Feed amount or molar flow of A</td><td>mol or mol/s</td></tr><tr><td>n_A</td><td>Unreacted amount or outlet molar flow of A</td><td>mol or mol/s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Feed and outlet quantities must use the same basis and time basis.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Single-reactant conversion" data-pw-title="Single-reactant conversion" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Steady-flow sensible energy change <span class="formula-category">Material &amp; energy balances</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">Q̇ = ṁ C_p (T_out − T_in)</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Q̇</td><td>Heat added to the stream</td><td>W</td></tr><tr><td>ṁ</td><td>Mass flow rate</td><td>kg/s</td></tr><tr><td>C_p</td><td>Specific heat capacity</td><td>J/(kg·K)</td></tr><tr><td>T</td><td>Temperature</td><td>K or °C for a difference</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Positive Q̇ adds heat to the stream. Assumes constant C_p and no phase change or shaft work.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Steady-flow sensible energy change" data-pw-title="Steady-flow sensible energy change" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Sensible heat for a fixed mass <span class="formula-category">Heat transfer</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">Q = m C_p ΔT</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Q</td><td>Heat added to or removed from the material</td><td>J</td></tr><tr><td>m</td><td>Material mass</td><td>kg</td></tr><tr><td>C_p</td><td>Specific heat capacity</td><td>J/(kg·K)</td></tr><tr><td>ΔT</td><td>Temperature change</td><td>K or °C difference</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Finite-mass sensible heating with constant heat capacity; excludes phase changes and heat losses.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Sensible heat for a fixed mass" data-pw-title="Sensible heat for a fixed mass" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Ideal gas law <span class="formula-category">Thermodynamics</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">P V = n R T</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>P</td><td>Absolute pressure</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>V</td><td>Volume</td><td>m³</td></tr><tr><td>n</td><td>Amount of substance</td><td>mol</td></tr><tr><td>R</td><td>Universal gas constant, 8.314462618</td><td>J/(mol·K)</td></tr><tr><td>T</td><td>Absolute temperature</td><td>K</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Approximation for gases at sufficiently low density; use absolute pressure and temperature.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Ideal gas law" data-pw-title="Ideal gas law" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Reynolds number <span class="formula-category">Fluid mechanics</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">Re = ρ v D / μ = v D / ν</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Re</td><td>Inertial-to-viscous force ratio</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>ρ</td><td>Fluid density</td><td>kg/m³</td></tr><tr><td>v</td><td>Mean velocity</td><td>m/s</td></tr><tr><td>D</td><td>Characteristic diameter</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>μ</td><td>Dynamic viscosity</td><td>Pa·s</td></tr><tr><td>ν</td><td>Kinematic viscosity</td><td>m²/s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For circular-pipe flow, Re below about 2,300 is commonly treated as laminar and above about 4,000 as turbulent; the interval is transitional.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Reynolds number" data-pw-title="Reynolds number" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Darcy–Weisbach pressure loss <span class="formula-category">Fluid mechanics</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">ΔP = f_D (L/D) (ρ v²/2)</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ΔP</td><td>Pressure drop</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>f_D</td><td>Darcy friction factor</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>L</td><td>Pipe length</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>D</td><td>Inside diameter</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>ρ</td><td>Fluid density</td><td>kg/m³</td></tr><tr><td>v</td><td>Mean velocity</td><td>m/s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Straight-pipe friction loss. Darcy friction factor is four times the Fanning friction factor.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Darcy–Weisbach pressure loss" data-pw-title="Darcy–Weisbach pressure loss" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Swamee–Jain friction-factor estimate <span class="formula-category">Fluid mechanics</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">f_D = 0.25 / [log₁₀(ε/(3.7D) + 5.74/Re⁰·⁹)]²</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>f_D</td><td>Darcy friction factor</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>ε</td><td>Absolute roughness</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>D</td><td>Pipe inside diameter</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>Re</td><td>Reynolds number</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Explicit turbulent-flow approximation. Do not use it for laminar flow; use f_D = 64/Re there.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Swamee–Jain friction-factor estimate" data-pw-title="Swamee–Jain friction-factor estimate" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Extended Bernoulli equation <span class="formula-category">Fluid mechanics</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">P₁/(ρg) + v₁²/(2g) + z₁ = P₂/(ρg) + v₂²/(2g) + z₂ + h_L</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>P</td><td>Static pressure</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>ρ</td><td>Fluid density</td><td>kg/m³</td></tr><tr><td>g</td><td>Gravitational acceleration, 9.80665</td><td>m/s²</td></tr><tr><td>v</td><td>Velocity</td><td>m/s</td></tr><tr><td>z</td><td>Elevation</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>h_L</td><td>Head loss</td><td>m</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Steady, incompressible flow along a streamline with losses represented as head. Add pump or turbine head when applicable.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Extended Bernoulli equation" data-pw-title="Extended Bernoulli equation" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Pump shaft power <span class="formula-category">Fluid mechanics</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">P_shaft = ρ g Q H / η</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>P_shaft</td><td>Required shaft power</td><td>W</td></tr><tr><td>ρ</td><td>Fluid density</td><td>kg/m³</td></tr><tr><td>g</td><td>Gravitational acceleration</td><td>m/s²</td></tr><tr><td>Q</td><td>Volumetric flow rate</td><td>m³/s</td></tr><tr><td>H</td><td>Pump head</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>η</td><td>Pump efficiency</td><td>dimensionless, 0–1</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Hydraulic power divided by efficiency. Excludes motor and drive losses unless included in η.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Pump shaft power" data-pw-title="Pump shaft power" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Fourier's law of heat conduction <span class="formula-category">Heat transfer</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">q'' = −k ∇T</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>q''</td><td>Heat flux vector</td><td>W/m²</td></tr><tr><td>k</td><td>Thermal conductivity</td><td>W/(m·K)</td></tr><tr><td>∇T</td><td>Temperature gradient</td><td>K/m</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Heat flows toward decreasing temperature. For a plane wall with constant k, Q̇ = k A (T₁ − T₂)/L.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Fourier's law of heat conduction" data-pw-title="Fourier's law of heat conduction" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Log-mean temperature difference <span class="formula-category">Heat transfer</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">ΔT_lm = (ΔT₁ − ΔT₂) / ln(ΔT₁/ΔT₂)</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ΔT_lm</td><td>Log-mean temperature difference</td><td>K</td></tr><tr><td>ΔT₁, ΔT₂</td><td>Terminal temperature differences</td><td>K</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Use positive terminal differences consistent with the exchanger flow arrangement. If both differences are equal, the limit is that common value.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Log-mean temperature difference" data-pw-title="Log-mean temperature difference" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Heat-exchanger design equation <span class="formula-category">Heat transfer</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">Q̇ = U A ΔT_lm</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Q̇</td><td>Heat-transfer rate</td><td>W</td></tr><tr><td>U</td><td>Overall heat-transfer coefficient</td><td>W/(m²·K)</td></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>Heat-transfer area</td><td>m²</td></tr><tr><td>ΔT_lm</td><td>Log-mean temperature difference</td><td>K</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Basic sizing relation; a correction factor may be required for multipass or cross-flow exchangers.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Heat-exchanger design equation" data-pw-title="Heat-exchanger design equation" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Fick's first law <span class="formula-category">Mass transfer</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">J_A = −D_AB ∇C_A</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>J_A</td><td>Molar diffusive flux of A</td><td>mol/(m²·s)</td></tr><tr><td>D_AB</td><td>Binary diffusivity</td><td>m²/s</td></tr><tr><td>∇C_A</td><td>Concentration gradient</td><td>mol/m⁴</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For one-dimensional steady diffusion through a film of thickness L, J_A ≈ −D_AB(C₂−C₁)/L.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Fick's first law" data-pw-title="Fick's first law" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Arrhenius equation <span class="formula-category">Reaction engineering</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">k = A exp(−E_a/(R T))</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>k</td><td>Rate constant</td><td>depends on reaction order</td></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>Pre-exponential factor</td><td>same units as k</td></tr><tr><td>E_a</td><td>Activation energy</td><td>J/mol</td></tr><tr><td>R</td><td>Universal gas constant</td><td>J/(mol·K)</td></tr><tr><td>T</td><td>Absolute temperature</td><td>K</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Use absolute temperature and an activation energy on the same molar basis as R.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Arrhenius equation" data-pw-title="Arrhenius equation" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Raoult's law <span class="formula-category">Thermodynamics</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">p_i = x_i P_i^sat</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>p_i</td><td>Partial pressure of component i</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>x_i</td><td>Liquid-phase mole fraction</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>P_i^sat</td><td>Pure-component saturation pressure</td><td>Pa</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ideal liquid-mixture approximation; total pressure is the sum of component partial pressures for an ideal vapor mixture.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Raoult's law" data-pw-title="Raoult's law" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Nusselt number <span class="formula-category">Heat transfer</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">Nu = h L_c / k</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nu</td><td>Convective-to-conductive heat-transfer ratio</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>h</td><td>Convective heat-transfer coefficient</td><td>W/(m²·K)</td></tr><tr><td>L_c</td><td>Characteristic length</td><td>m</td></tr><tr><td>k</td><td>Fluid thermal conductivity</td><td>W/(m·K)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Correlations for Nu depend on geometry, flow regime, and boundary conditions.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Nusselt number" data-pw-title="Nusselt number" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Prandtl number <span class="formula-category">Heat transfer</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">Pr = μ C_p / k</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pr</td><td>Momentum-to-thermal diffusivity ratio</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>μ</td><td>Dynamic viscosity</td><td>Pa·s</td></tr><tr><td>C_p</td><td>Specific heat capacity</td><td>J/(kg·K)</td></tr><tr><td>k</td><td>Thermal conductivity</td><td>W/(m·K)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A fluid property group that compares momentum and thermal diffusion.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Prandtl number" data-pw-title="Prandtl number" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>Batch first-order kinetics <span class="formula-category">Reaction engineering</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">C_A/C_A,0 = exp(−k t);  X_A = 1 − exp(−k t)</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>C_A</td><td>Reactant concentration at time t</td><td>mol/m³</td></tr><tr><td>C_A,0</td><td>Initial reactant concentration</td><td>mol/m³</td></tr><tr><td>k</td><td>First-order rate constant</td><td>s⁻¹</td></tr><tr><td>t</td><td>Time</td><td>s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Applies to an irreversible first-order reaction in a constant-volume batch system.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="Batch first-order kinetics" data-pw-title="Batch first-order kinetics" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>First-order CSTR conversion <span class="formula-category">Reaction engineering</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">X_A = k τ / (1 + k τ)</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>X_A</td><td>Reactant conversion</td><td>dimensionless</td></tr><tr><td>k</td><td>First-order rate constant</td><td>s⁻¹</td></tr><tr><td>τ</td><td>Space time / residence time</td><td>s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Steady-state, isothermal ideal CSTR with constant density and first-order kinetics.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="First-order CSTR conversion" data-pw-title="First-order CSTR conversion" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article><article class="card formula-card"><h3>First-order step response <span class="formula-category">Process control</span></h3><div class="formula-equation">y(t) = y₀ + K Δu [1 − exp(−t/τ)]</div><table class="variable-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>y₀</td><td>Initial output</td><td>output units</td></tr><tr><td>K</td><td>Process gain</td><td>output/input</td></tr><tr><td>Δu</td><td>Input step</td><td>input units</td></tr><tr><td>τ</td><td>Time constant</td><td>s</td></tr><tr><td>t</td><td>Elapsed time</td><td>s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Monotonic response of a stable first-order process to a step input.</p><button type="button" class="pw-pin-card" data-pw-pin="" data-pw-page="formulas" data-pw-target="First-order step response" data-pw-title="First-order step response" title="Pin to Favorites">☆</button></article></div></div></section>
